doc/ - LaTeX report
===================

IEEE-conference report of the configurable mesh, protocol, C API, dataflow
mappings, timing requirements and reproducible wire-cost experiments.
Functional verification, wire counters and a real Vivado 2026.1 synthesis/STA
run are available (verification/2026-09-23/vivado). The default 4x4 Nexys A7
passes a 10 ns constraint with STEP_DIV=2. Other configurations, physical-link
latency, power and board acceptance remain to be evaluated.

Layout
------
    main.tex        minimal assembly of front matter, sections and references
    frontmatter/    title/author, abstract, keywords
    backmatter/     bibliography placement and final-page balancing
    config/         packages, colours, TikZ styles and PDF links
    src/            section entry points + one topic per nested file
    figures/        one directory per figure: diagram.tex + figure.tex
    tables/         one directory per table: table.tex
    bib/bib.bib     sole bibliography source
    IEEEtran.cls    existing vendored document class
    IEEEtran.bst    unmodified vendored BibTeX style (THIRD_PARTY.md)
    tools/          workload runner, CSV renderer and isolated preview builder
    data/           measured CSV plus source/compiler provenance
    verification/   archived commands, logs and bibliography checks
    build/main.pdf  canonical rebuilt report; build/ is generated
    main.pdf        historical tracked copy; not updated by the build
    mesh-generalization.md  supported shapes, scope and remaining work

Bibliography
------------
Edit bib/bib.bib only. main.tex uses BibTeX with the vendored IEEEtran.bst;
latexmk regenerates build/main.bbl when citations or entries change. The old
hand-maintained bib.tex duplicate has been removed. Only cited entries are
printed; unused database entries are allowed. DOI URLs make references
clickable with this style. Verification notes and remaining source caveats:
verification/2026-09-22/report/bibliography.md.

Build (from the repository root)
--------------------------------
    make doc                         -> doc/build/main.pdf
    make -C doc -f doc.mk measure     -> explicitly replace data/wire-cost.*
    make -C doc -f doc.mk clean       -> remove generated build/

An ordinary PDF build renders its table and chart from the archived CSV,
checks its provenance hash, and does not rerun the experiment. The measurement
runner compares each kernel with a scalar reference before emitting counts;
the Python script checks analytical transaction/byte totals. Counts exclude
initial ID and include one successful call per workload, with CFG and compute.
The report and metadata describe this scope; there is no serial-time model.
The metadata identifies the measured source snapshot by hashes even in a dirty
tree. Later source changes require a deliberate rerun to claim current data.

Atomic editing: see STRUCTURE.md for the topic/asset map and AGENTS.md for the
focused editing workflow. For example:

    make -C doc -f doc.mk figure-pe
    make -C doc -f doc.mk section-protocol
    make -C doc -f doc.mk part UNIT=protocol/fused-execute

Artifacts are under build/previews/KIND/NAME/preview.pdf. Previews use the
report's fonts and styles; figures/tables include captions. Cross-section
reference numbers use the last full build when available. Run make doc after
editing labels/order and before treating the complete PDF as final.

Dependencies: GNU make 4.3+, Python 3, latexmk, BibTeX and TeX Live with hyperref, bookmark,
TikZ, pgfplots, booktabs, array, microtype and xr (TeX Live tools bundle). Measurement also needs a C11
compiler and make. `nix develop` and `nix build .#doc` provide the report
packages. Nix's Git flake source includes tracked files only; newly added
sources must be included in the source snapshot for a packaged build.

Figures stay as source. The report has PDF bookmarks and clickable citations.
Review the final log for missing references, BibTeX warnings and overfull boxes,
and inspect rendered pages after changing diagrams or column layout.
